# The released dataset must check out byte-identical on every platform, or the
# digests in dataset/SHA256SUMS fail and the CSV silently changes size. On a
# Windows machine with core.autocrlf=true every text file here was being
# rewritten to CRLF on checkout, which made `sha256sum -c` unable to parse its
# own file list and added one byte per line to export.csv. Verified on a fresh
# clone 2026-09-15; fixed here rather than in a note asking readers to set git
# config, which they would not do.
dataset/**          text eol=lf
dataset/*.sqlite    binary

# Source and docs: normalise to LF in the repository so diffs are not noise.
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
